file.path is the normal solution. People seem to show it with the sep set,
but I think the whole point is it knows what separator to use so:

file.path("first folder" , "second_folder" , "file.name")

file.path(getwd(), "subfolder", "file.name")

Should both work across any platform. But it may forward slash them on
windows, since that usually works. UNC folders are a PITA on R in general
in my experience.

Since R 4.0 you can use a raw string using r"( the string )". E.g.

r"(C:\windows\system32)"

And this returns - "C:\\windows\\system32"

Which seems to be the question the OP asked, even if it might not have been
the question they wanted to ask.

